#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:76
msgid ""
"Served by the MLX vision engine, the one that runs multimodal models such as"
" Gemma 4. The drafter is validated against the target when the model loads."
msgstr ""
"Lo sirve el motor de visión MLX, que ejecuta modelos multimodales como Gemma"
" 4. El borrador se valida contra el objetivo al cargar."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:79
msgid ":ref:`llama.cpp <llama_cpp_backend>`"
msgstr ":ref:`llama.cpp <llama_cpp_backend>`"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:80
msgid "``xllamacpp>=2026.6.9713``"
msgstr "``xllamacpp>=2026.6.9713``"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:81
msgid ""
"Translated into the ``draft-mtp`` speculative implementation. The drafter is"
" a single gguf published inside the target's own repository, so its "
"quantizations are its own (``BF16``, ``F16``, ``Q8_0`` for Gemma 4) and "
"independent of the target's. Earlier llama.cpp builds do not know the "
"``gemma4-assistant`` architecture and cannot load it."
msgstr ""
"Se traduce a ``draft-mtp``. El borrador es un solo gguf en el repositorio "
"del objetivo; sus cuantizaciones (``BF16``, ``F16``, ``Q8_0`` para Gemma 4) "
"son independientes de las del objetivo. Versiones antiguas de llama.cpp no "
"reconocen ``gemma4-assistant`` y no pueden cargarlo."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:87
msgid ""
"Not supported by the Transformers engine: it runs its own continuous-"
"batching loop rather than ``generate()``, so there is nowhere to attach a "
"drafter."
msgstr ""
"El motor Transformers no lo admite: utiliza su propio bucle de batching "
"continuo en lugar de ``generate()``, sin punto para conectar un borrador."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:91
msgid "TRT-LLM"
msgstr "TRT-LLM"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:95
msgid ""
"Ordinary TRT-LLM replicas support NGram and Draft/Target speculative "
"decoding with ``tensorrt-llm==1.2.1`` on Linux/CUDA. Model architectures and"
" checkpoint formats follow :ref:`trt_llm_backend`, with TP=PP=CP=1. Xavier "
"shared caching, native P/D and Xavier P/D do not support speculation through"
" this adapter; see :ref:`user_guide_pd_separation` for their supported "
"configurations."
msgstr ""
"Las réplicas normales TRT-LLM admiten NGram y Draft/Target con ``tensorrt-"
"llm==1.2.1`` en Linux/CUDA. Las arquitecturas y los formatos siguen "
":ref:`trt_llm_backend`, con TP=PP=CP=1. La caché compartida Xavier, P/D "
"nativo y P/D Xavier no admiten decodificación especulativa mediante este "
"adaptador; consulte las configuraciones compatibles en "
":ref:`user_guide_pd_separation`."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:101
msgid ""
"NGram reuses token patterns from the prompt and generated text without "
"loading a draft model. For a workload with repeated text, pass the native "
"``speculative_config`` at launch:"
msgstr ""
"NGram reutiliza patrones de tokens del prompt y del texto generado sin "
"cargar un modelo borrador. Para cargas con texto repetido, pase la "
"configuración nativa ``speculative_config`` al iniciar:"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:131
msgid ""
"Draft/Target loads a separate draft model. Provide its local checkpoint path"
" with ``draft_model_path``; ``num_speculative_tokens`` maps to TRT's "
"``max_draft_len`` and defaults to ``3``. This counts draft tokens and "
"excludes the target's bonus token. The draft and target must have compatible"
" tokenizers and vocabularies, and both must be supported by TRT-LLM 1.2.1. "
"Use a smaller dense Qwen3 checkpoint for the draft when serving a larger "
"dense Qwen3 target. This mode does not require the Gemma-style paired "
"assistant or a shared KV cache."
msgstr ""
"Draft/Target carga un modelo borrador independiente. Indique su checkpoint "
"local con ``draft_model_path``; ``num_speculative_tokens`` corresponde a "
"``max_draft_len`` de TRT y vale ``3`` por defecto. Cuenta tokens borrador "
"sin incluir el token adicional del objetivo. Ambos modelos deben tener "
"tokenizadores y vocabularios compatibles y ser admitidos por TRT-LLM 1.2.1. "
"Use un checkpoint Qwen3 denso más pequeño como borrador de un objetivo Qwen3"
" denso mayor. Este modo no requiere un assistant emparejado de Gemma ni "
"compartir la caché KV."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:148
msgid ""
"The examples require a compatible TRT-LLM environment. Change the model "
"sizes and draft path to checkpoints available on your worker. A draft "
"consumes additional GPU memory and compute, so it may reduce throughput at "
"high load."
msgstr ""
"Los ejemplos requieren un entorno TRT-LLM compatible. Ajuste los tamaños y "
"la ruta del borrador a los checkpoints de su worker. El borrador consume "
"memoria GPU y cómputo adicionales y puede reducir el rendimiento bajo carga "
"elevada."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:152
msgid ""
"An explicit ``speculative_config`` takes precedence over "
"``draft_model_path`` and ``num_speculative_tokens``. The adapter defaults "
"``disable_overlap_scheduler=True`` when speculation is configured. Use "
"native TRT options only with combinations supported by the pinned runtime. "
"EAGLE3 and model-specific MTP require the corresponding architecture and "
"speculative checkpoint configuration. ``enable_mtp=True`` downloads the "
"compatible drafter declared in the Xinference model spec and configures "
"Draft/Target unless ``speculative_config`` overrides it."
msgstr ""
"Un ``speculative_config`` explícito tiene prioridad sobre "
"``draft_model_path`` y ``num_speculative_tokens``. El adaptador usa "
"``disable_overlap_scheduler=True`` de forma predeterminada al configurar "
"especulación. Use opciones nativas de TRT solo con combinaciones admitidas "
"por la versión fijada. EAGLE3 y MTP específico del modelo requieren la "
"arquitectura y la configuración de checkpoint especulativo correspondientes."
" ``enable_mtp=True`` descarga el borrador compatible declarado en la "
"especificación Xinference y configura Draft/Target, salvo que "
"``speculative_config`` lo reemplace."

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:161
msgid "When it pays off"
msgstr "Cuándo compensa"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:162
msgid ""
"Speculation is only worth it when a drafting step is cheap *relative to* a "
"target decoding step. The drafter is a small dense model whose cost does not"
" change with the target, so the ratio is what decides the outcome — and a "
"mixture-of-experts target can land on the wrong side of it, because only its"
" activated slice is read per token:"
msgstr ""
"La especulación solo compensa si cada paso de borrador es barato *respecto "
"a* un paso del objetivo. El borrador es un modelo denso pequeño de coste "
"fijo, por lo que importa la proporción. Un objetivo de mezcla de expertos "
"puede resultar desfavorable, pues solo lee su parte activada por token:"

#: ../../source/user_guide/speculative_decoding.rst:172
msgid "gemma-4 MLX, 4bit, M5 Pro"
msgstr "gemma-4 MLX, 4bit, M5 Pro"

